From: gstreamer-custom-build local patches
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: read the "auto-resize" property as a boolean

"auto-resize" is registered with g_param_spec_boolean() but the setter reads
it with g_value_get_uint(). That fails the G_VALUE_HOLDS_UINT assertion and
returns 0, so the property is silently forced to FALSE no matter what the
application sets:

    (gst-launch-1.0:64380): GLib-GObject-CRITICAL **: g_value_get_uint:
        assertion 'G_VALUE_HOLDS_UINT (value)' failed

Reproduce with any value, integer or boolean:

    gst-launch-1.0 videotestsrc num-buffers=5 \
      ! dwritetextoverlay text="a" auto-resize=true ! fakesink

The getter at PROP_AUTO_RESIZE already uses g_value_set_boolean(), so reading
the property back reports whatever priv->auto_resize holds - which is always
the default. The result is that font-size is applied literally at the frame
resolution instead of being scaled relative to "reference-frame-size", and the
caller gets no indication that the request was dropped.

Found while overlaying camera names on 1920x1080 sources composited onto a 4K
video wall: the titles never scaled, and every pipeline start logged the
assertion above.

Still present in 1.28.5 and in main as of 1.29.2.1.
--- a/_p2_/sys/dwrite/gstdwritebaseoverlay.cpp
+++ b/_p2_/sys/dwrite/gstdwritebaseoverlay.cpp
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@
     }
     case PROP_AUTO_RESIZE:
     {
-      gboolean auto_resize = g_value_get_uint (value);
+      gboolean auto_resize = g_value_get_boolean (value);
       if (auto_resize != priv->auto_resize) {
         priv->auto_resize = auto_resize;
         priv->text_format = nullptr;
